 ## Subtopics
 
+### [EmissivityRenderer](4811-emissivityrenderer.md)
+A differentiable volume renderer for multi-line neural tomography that recovers 3-D coronal electron density and temperature from multiview spectral-intensity images. It distinguishes itself by applying to solar coronal physics with CHIANTI atomic data, unlike general differential CT methods. [EmissivityRenderer](4811-emissivityrenderer.md)
+
+### [Differential Rendering for CT Reconstruction](6462-differential-rendering-for-ct-reconstruction.md)
+An inverse rendering technique reconstructing volumetric absorption coefficients from 2D X-ray projections via gradient descent on MSE loss. It uses fully auto-differentiable rendering engines with a fixed 45° multi-view rotation strategy and ADAM optimization, differing from voxel-based approaches like DiffVox. [Differential Rendering for CT Reconstruction](6462-differential-rendering-for-ct-reconstruction.md)
+
+### [DiffVox](10071-diffvox.md)
+A self-supervised Cone-Beam CT reconstruction framework optimizing a discrete voxel grid using physics-based differentiable rendering (Siddon's or trilinear interpolation). It targets sparse-view reconstruction with faster runtimes than neural fields, avoiding artifacts common in traditional iterative methods. [DiffVox](10071-diffvox.md)
+
 ### Attenuation-based Rendering
-A rendering equation adapted for X-ray tomography where intensity is attenuated along the ray path, rather than emitted/reflected. It assumes symmetry along the ray (reversing bounds does not change intensity). The rendered intensity is $I = I_0 \exp(-\int \mu(s) ds)$, where $I_0$ is source intensity and $\mu(s)$ is the density/attenuation coefficient [S2, unofficial]. Implementation steps include: 1. Conceptually fixing the sample at the origin and rotating the camera; 2. Calculating attenuation along the ray using the canonical density field; 3. Outputting monochromatic intensity (RGB channels identical); 4. Adding a trainable flat field background to account for non-saturated detector response [S2, unofficial].
